      "raw_answer": "{\n  \"sections\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"my-orders-status-filter\",\n      \"title\": \"my_orders now excludes cancelled orders from the user's own order list\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The single hunk adds a second predicate (Order.status != \\\"cancelled\\\") to the existing ownership-scoped query in my_orders. This is a data-visibility change to the /orders/mine endpoint: it narrows which of the caller's own orders are returned. The authorization concern is that the endpoint's contract (api-spec.md: 'own orders only') and the security policy (security-policy.md \u00a73: 'A user may view ONLY their own orders') do not mention any status-based exclusion, and no code path in the base or PR snapshot ever sets status to 'cancelled' (grep for 'cancel' returns no matches outside this new line). The change therefore introduces an undocumented, unenforced filter that silently hides the user's own cancelled orders, and the literal 'cancelled' is not a value produced anywhere in the codebase. It is grouped as one access-control concern because it alters the set of records a user is permitted to see on their own endpoint.\",\n      \"hunks\": [\"app/routes/orders.py#0\"],\n      \"context\": [\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/orders.py\", \"symbol\": \"my_orders\", \"start_line\": 36, \"end_line\": 47, \"snapshot\": \"pr\", \"why\": \"The changed function; shows the new filter on line 43 and the @require_auth decorator that sets g.current_user.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/models.py\", \"symbol\": \"Order\", \"start_line\": 43, \"end_line\": 62, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Defines Order.status (String(20), default 'pending') and to_dict which returns status; confirms 'cancelled' is not a default or documented value.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"require_auth\", \"start_line\": 55, \"end_line\": 66, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Decorator that authenticates the caller and sets g.current_user used by the ownership filter.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"security-policy.md\", \"symbol\": \"\u00a73 Order data access rules\", \"start_line\": 27, \"end_line\": 34, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Authoritative rule that a user may view only their own orders; no status-based exclusion is specified.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"api-spec.md\", \"symbol\": \"Orders table\", \"start_line\": 30, \"end_line\": 36, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Documents GET /orders/mine as 'own orders only' with no mention of excluding cancelled orders.\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
