      "raw_answer": "The changed line adds a status filter (`Order.status != \"cancelled\")` to the `my_orders` endpoint. I verified:\n\n- The endpoint is properly authenticated via `@require_auth` (app/auth.py:55-66) and scoped to the caller's own orders via `Order.user_id == g.current_user.id` \u2014 satisfying security-policy.md \u00a73 (\"A user may view ONLY their own orders\").\n- The new filter is a data-visibility restriction, not an authorization check. It does not weaken ownership scoping, does not introduce a user-controlled identifier, and does not bypass any role/ownership check.\n- The policy and API spec do not mandate returning cancelled orders, so excluding them is not a policy violation.\n\nNo IDOR, missing authorization, or incorrect authorization is introduced by this change.\n\n{\n  \"findings\": []\n}",
